---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import Figure from "@/components/Figure.astro";
import DotChart from "@/components/DotChart.astro";
import { ARMS, SUMMARY_BY_ID, deskTasks, buildTasks, processTasks, processCampaign, PROCESS_PILOT, provenance, findings, intervals, deskComparison, REPO, SITE, ORG, AUTHORS, RELEASE, REPS, fmt } from "@/lib/data";
const desk = deskTasks(), build = buildTasks(), proc = processTasks(), pilot = processCampaign(PROCESS_PILOT);
const F = Object.fromEntries(ARMS.map((a) => [a.id, findings(a.id)]));
const I = Object.fromEntries(ARMS.map((a) => [a.id, intervals(a.id)]));
const comparison = deskComparison(), bs = provenance().paired_task_bootstrap;
const attemptsTotal = ARMS.reduce((n, a) => n + SUMMARY_BY_ID[a.id].attempts, 0);
const desc = `Evaluate AI agents on complete business deliverables. Inspect ${desk.length} desk tasks and ${fmt.int(attemptsTotal)} recorded attempts, unscored application tasks, and a separate ERP process pilot.`;
const cite = `@misc{businessbench2026,
  title        = {Business Bench: Evaluating Agents on Business Deliverables},
  author       = {${AUTHORS.map((a) => { const p = a.split(" "); return `${p.slice(1).join(" ")}, ${p[0]}`; }).join(" and ")}},
  year         = {2026},
  howpublished = {\\url{${SITE}}},
  note         = {Desk release ${RELEASE.id}}
}`;
const jsonld = [
  { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "WebSite", name: "Business Bench", url: SITE + "/", publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: ORG.name, url: ORG.url } },
  { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Dataset", name: "Business Bench desk comparison", url: SITE + "/results", description: desc,
    version: RELEASE.version, datePublished: RELEASE.date, isAccessibleForFree: true, license: `${REPO}/blob/main/LICENSE`,
    creator: [{ "@type": "Organization", name: ORG.name, url: ORG.url }],
    variableMeasured: ["attempt acceptance", "all-three acceptance", "required-check completion", "wall time", "captured model cost"],
    distribution: [{ "@type": "DataDownload", encodingFormat: "application/x-ndjson", contentUrl: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/erphq/business-bench/main/results/latest/attempts.jsonl` }],
  },
];
---
<Base title="Business Bench" description={desc} path="/" jsonld={jsonld}>
  <nav slot="contents" class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
    <span class="toc-h">On this page</span>
    <a href="#abstract">The measurement problem</a><a href="#tracks">What is available</a><a href="#figure-1">Desk comparison</a>
    <a href="#findings">What changes the conclusion</a><a href="#grading">Inspect the evidence</a><a href="#cite">Cite</a>
  </nav>
  <h1>Business Bench</h1>
  <p class="meta">Public tasks, executable evaluation and recorded attempts<span class="sep">·</span>MIT licence</p>
  <p class="lede">Business Bench evaluates AI agents through the files and system state they produce: reconciled workbooks, usable imports, supported reports, and transactions that respect the company’s rules.</p>
  <p class="byline">{AUTHORS.join(", ")} · {ORG.name} Research</p>
  <div class="article-links"><a href="/results">Inspect the results</a><a href="/tasks">Explore the tasks</a><a href="/paper">Read the paper</a></div>

  <section class="abstract" aria-labelledby="abstract">
    <h2 id="abstract">The measurement problem</h2>
    <p>A deliverable can satisfy most checks and still fail its purpose. A balanced workbook may omit a customer; a correct payment may violate an approval rule. Each task therefore declares an <strong>acceptance contract</strong>: the required artifact or state, the properties that matter, and the checks used to accept it.</p>
    <p>Three questions must stay separate. <strong>Acceptance</strong> asks whether the declared checks pass. <strong>Repeatability</strong> asks whether another execution passes on the same inputs. <strong>Validity</strong> asks whether the checks capture the recipient’s actual requirements. The benchmark measures the first two; its public tasks and scoring rules make the third open to inspection and dispute.</p>
  </section>

  <h2 id="tracks">What is available</h2>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th>Track</th><th>Unit of work</th><th>Evaluation</th><th>Published evidence</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><a href="/tasks#desk"><b>Desk</b></a><br />{desk.length} tasks</td><td>A file workspace becomes a set of deliverables.</td><td>Executable checks on keys, values, recalculated workbooks and declared text rules.</td><td><a href="/results">{fmt.int(attemptsTotal)} attempts</a><br />{ARMS.length} configured systems, {REPS} repetitions per task.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="/tasks#build"><b>Build</b></a><br />{build.length} task packs</td><td>A running application, followed by three changes.</td><td>A tester checks the application against its acceptance checklist and a shared enterprise baseline.</td><td><strong>No published scores.</strong><br />Specifications and validation of task packs.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="/process"><b>Process</b></a><br />{proc.length} tasks</td><td>A role in an ERP over several business dates.</td><td>Checks on final state, declared audit rules, account ties and handoff notes.</td><td><a href="/process#campaign">{pilot.tasks.length}-task pilot, {pilot.attempts.length} attempts</a><br />Local execution; practitioner review pending.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>These tracks test different objects under different protocols. Their scores are not pooled. The current process inventory includes tasks absent from the published pilot.</p>

  <h2 id="desk-comparison">A complete desk comparison</h2>
  <p>On the released {desk.length} tasks, Proto with DeepSeek V4.1 Flash passes {SUMMARY_BY_ID["proto-deepseek"].passed}/{SUMMARY_BY_ID["proto-deepseek"].attempts} attempts; Codex with GPT-5.6-sol passes {SUMMARY_BY_ID["codex-sol"].passed}/{SUMMARY_BY_ID["codex-sol"].attempts}. The model, harness, provider configuration and cohort dates vary together. This comparison describes two configured systems on an exposed workload.</p>
  <Figure n={1} id="figure-1">
    <DotChart
      label={`Desk acceptance and all-three acceptance: ${ARMS.map((a) => `${a.system}: ${fmt.pct(I[a.id].pass1.value)} of attempts, ${fmt.pct(I[a.id].passAll.value)} of tasks in all three repetitions`).join("; ")}.`}
      domain={[0.6, 1]} ticks={[0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 0.9, 1]}
      keys={[{ label: "Accepted attempts", shape: "" }, { label: `Tasks accepted in all ${REPS} repetitions`, shape: "ring" }]}
      rows={ARMS.map((a) => ({
        label: a.system, sub: a.harness, slot: a.slot, link: true,
        points: [
          { value: I[a.id].pass1.value, lo: I[a.id].pass1.ci[0], hi: I[a.id].pass1.ci[1], title: `Accepted attempts ${fmt.pct(I[a.id].pass1.value)}` },
          { value: I[a.id].passAll.value, lo: I[a.id].passAll.ci[0], hi: I[a.id].passAll.ci[1], shape: "ring", title: `All-three acceptance ${fmt.pct(I[a.id].passAll.value)}` },
        ], valueText: fmt.pct(I[a.id].pass1.value), valueSub: `all three ${fmt.pct(I[a.id].passAll.value)}`,
      }))}
    />
    <Fragment slot="caption">Desk release <code>{RELEASE.id}</code>. All {fmt.int(attemptsTotal)} attempts use the shared retrospective scorer. Whiskers are descriptive 95% task-bootstrap intervals, retaining each task’s repetitions. The paired attempt-rate gap is {bs.difference_percentage_points.toFixed(2)} percentage points (interval {bs.bootstrap_95_percent_interval_pp.map((n: number) => n.toFixed(2)).join(" to ")}). These intervals exclude evaluator selection, related task families and deployment shift. <a href="/results">Inspect counts and conditions</a>.</Fragment>
  </Figure>

  <h2 id="findings">What changes the conclusion</h2>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th>Observation</th><th>Interpretation</th><th>Inspect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Mean check completion is {fmt.pct(F["proto-deepseek"].meanCheckFraction, 2)} and {fmt.pct(F["codex-sol"].meanCheckFraction, 2)}.</td><td>Completing most requirements is more common than completing the whole declared contract. Check granularity also changes partial-credit scores.</td><td><a href="/analysis#conjunctive-gap">Acceptance boundary</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>All-three acceptance is {fmt.pct(F["proto-deepseek"].passAll)} and {fmt.pct(F["codex-sol"].passAll)}.</td><td>Repeated execution exposes instability on fixed fixtures; it does not test new cases or establish a deployment failure rate.</td><td><a href="/analysis#reliability">Repeatability</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Equal category weights change the gap from {(comparison.frozenDifference * 100).toFixed(2)} to {(comparison.equalCategories.difference * 100).toFixed(2)} points.</td><td>The overall ordering depends on which work is represented. Reports and drafting account for more than the net advantage.</td><td><a href="/analysis#divergence">Workload sensitivity</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Scorer changes shift the between-system gap by {(comparison.scorerSensitivity * 100).toFixed(2)} points on the same outputs.</td><td>A reproducible scorer can still make contestable measurement choices. Evaluator changes are distinct from agent improvements.</td><td><a href="/audit#grading-validity">Evaluator sensitivity</a></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <div class="callout warn"><span class="t">Who produced the evidence</span><p>{ORG.name} publishes Business Bench and develops Proto. The primary desk scorer was frozen after outputs existed and increased Proto’s measured lead. The public ledger preserves original and revised verdicts; historical raw artifacts are not all public. The <a href="/audit">evidence audit</a> distinguishes what can be verified from what still needs independent review.</p></div>

  <h2 id="grading">Inspect the evidence</h2>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th>Your question</th><th>Start here</th><th>What it can establish</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>What was the agent asked to do?</td><td><a href="/tasks/payments-match-v2">A worked desk task</a>; <a href="/process/procure-to-pay-week">a process episode</a></td><td>Inputs, rules, expected handoff, and declared checks.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Do the published numbers reconcile?</td><td><a href="/reproduce">Verify the release</a>; <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/results/latest/attempts.jsonl`} rel="noopener">desk ledger</a></td><td>Complete recorded matrices, totals and recorded evidence fingerprints.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Do the tests measure useful work?</td><td><a href="/methods">Measurement protocol</a>; <a href="/audit">validity and audit limits</a></td><td>The current contract and controls; independent artifact adjudication remains an open requirement.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>What would strengthen the result?</td><td><a href="/roadmap">Research roadmap</a>; <a href="/paper">paper</a></td><td>Prospective evaluator review, held-out work, matched comparisons and human baselines.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2 id="cite">Cite</h2>
  <pre class="cite" aria-label="BibTeX citation">{cite}</pre>
  <p class="muted">Name the campaign and scorer when citing a result. The website combines ledger-derived statistics, task-source metadata and explanatory analysis; their provenance is linked where used. <a href={`${REPO}/issues`} rel="noopener">Report a task or measurement dispute</a> with the task ID, declared rule and evidence needed to reproduce it.</p>
</Base>
